Syntax: cast 'dispel invisible' <target>

Dispel Invisible strips away magical concealment from a creature or object,
revealing it to normal sight. The spell unravels the enchantment that bends
light around the target, making the invisible visible once more.

The caster must be able to perceive the target in some way to cast this
spell - typically through detect invisible, true sight, or other magical
means. Casting dispel invisible on a target that is already visible has
no effect (and may elicit some confused looks from bystanders).

The spell permanently removes the invisibility effect rather than merely
suppressing it. The target must be made invisible again through another
casting to regain concealment. This makes dispel invisible valuable for
exposing sneaky opponents or revealing hidden objects.

See Also: INVISIBILITY, DETECT INVISIBLE, FAERIE FOG
